===Sports===
The New Jersey sports plates were introduced in the fall of 2010. They share a common serial format – {{small|R/M}}12AB – and were the first NJ plates to be issued with screened, rather than embossed, serials.
{|class="wikitable"
!Image
!Type
!Notes
|-
|[[File:Blank License Plate Shape.svg|150px]]
|[[NASCAR]]
|Plates feature the number and signature of one of the following eight drivers: [[Dale Earnhardt]], [[Dale Earnhardt Jr.]], [[Danica Patrick]], [[Jeff Gordon]], [[Jimmie Johnson]], [[Kevin Harvick]], [[Martin Truex Jr.]] and [[Tony Stewart]]. There is also a Dale Earnhardt Hall of Fame commemorative plate, a [[Ford Racing]] plate and a generic NASCAR Fan plate.
|-
|[[File:Blank License Plate Shape.svg|150px]]
|[[National Basketball Association|NBA]]
|Plates feature the logo of either the [[New York Knicks]] or the [[Philadelphia 76ers]].<ref>[http://www.state.nj.us/mvc/Vehicle/nba.htm NBA License Plates], New Jersey Motor Vehicle Commission. Retrieved 2010-11-21.</ref> There was also a [[New Jersey Nets]] plate, which was discontinued when the Nets moved to Brooklyn in 2012.
|-
|[[File:Blank License Plate Shape.svg|150px]]
|[[National Hockey League|NHL]]
|Plates feature the logo of either the [[New Jersey Devils]] or the [[Philadelphia Flyers]].<ref>[http://www.state.nj.us/mvc/Vehicle/nhl.htm NHL License Plates], New Jersey Motor Vehicle Commission. Retrieved 2012-08-14.</ref>
|-
|[[File:Blank License Plate Shape.svg|150px]]
|[[Major League Baseball|MLB]]
